bridge/log/

# the pilot benchmark data is experiment evidence — keep it
!bridge/log/*.json

# harvested machine blocks and container templates must travel - a clean clone has to build (2026-10-01)
!exports/*_block_*.gcode
!exports/*block*.gcode
!exports/*container*.gcode.3mf
!exports/ender_start.gcode
!exports/ender_end.gcode

# STOLICA is a 170 mm body: its STL (179 MB), geometry dump (35 MB) and raw G-code (66 MB) are
# reproducible from core/weft_field_geometry.mjs. The sliced container and the evidence travel;
# the bulk does not. Rebuild command and SHA-256 are in the specimen README (2026-10-02).
specimens/2026-10-02_stolica_A1/STOLICA.stl
specimens/2026-10-02_stolica_A1/STOLICA_geometry.json
specimens/2026-10-02_stolica_A1/STOLICA.gcode

# The Ender cut of the three full bodies: display STLs (21/7/4.5 MB) and geometry dumps (8/3/2.6 MB)
# are reproducible from core/weft_solid_geometry.mjs. Toolpaths and evidence travel; the bulk does
# not. Rebuild commands and SHA-256 are in the specimen README/manifest (2026-10-02).
specimens/2026-10-02_pure_weft_ENDER/*.stl
specimens/2026-10-02_pure_weft_ENDER/*_geometry.json

# SOKOL, both cuts: 188 mm and 280 mm. Same reason — the container and the G-code are the delivery,
# the mesh and the field dump are a rebuild away (core/weft_field_geometry.mjs).
specimens/2026-10-02_sokol_A1/SOKOL.stl
specimens/2026-10-02_sokol_A1/SOKOL_geometry.json
specimens/2026-10-02_sokol_A1/SOKOL.gcode
specimens/2026-10-02_sokol_A2L/SOKOL.stl
specimens/2026-10-02_sokol_A2L/SOKOL_geometry.json
specimens/2026-10-02_sokol_A2L/SOKOL.gcode
